| `make lint-sh` `[local]` | Lints every shell script a commit could carry with the linter `shell.linter` names, through `scripts/shell_gate.py`; a file is a shell script by its suffix or its shebang. It rides `make lint`. | `make lint-sh` | [`shell.enabled`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`shell.excluded_paths`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`shell.no_scripts`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`shell.linter`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`shell.script_suffixes`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`shell.shebang_shells`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | Exit 11 naming the tool when it is on neither the interpreter's directory nor PATH, never a skip; keel installs no shell tool. A project with no shell file is exit 13 unless `shell.no_scripts` states the reason, which it prints before it exits 0, and a reason left beside a shell file is exit 14; `shell.enabled` false says so and exits 0. Does not judge test files. | [deterministic-checks.md](../guides/deterministic-checks.md) | always |
